From cdfc014885af4d349875a442a8ebcaf5ed2b8217 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yooz <136268860+y-o-o-z@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 19:13:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/14] local: erssi journal hardening after review

- tail: a read error never becomes an unhandled rejection (poll catches per
  file), bytesRead is honoured, rotation is detected by inode as well as by
  size and the old file's last lines are read from <file>.1; prime() takes
  the size once, window names come from the end of the file only
- setup: a superseded setup stops before each channel and never writes,
  each setup has its own backfilled set; the late start (networks without
  init) runs after 3 s only if no init came, and loads the windows' history
  before they are sent; a new network's lobby is sent with its history
- init: a storage error in the journal setup is logged, not fatal
- erssi windows refuse window-scoped commands (/close, /clear, /window...),
  which fe-web would run on the terminal's open window
- cache busting memoized on the mtime of bundle.js (a rebuild without a
  restart gets new URLs), loading-error-handlers.js included
- fe-web disconnect: nothing to wait for on a closed socket

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
